    excerpt: "Thirteen nights. One venue. More ink on stage than most comedy festivals see in a decade. Pins & Needles Comedy \u2014 New York City's tattoo-culture stand-up showcase \u2014 just wrapped a run at the\u2026",
    body: "Thirteen nights. One venue. More ink on stage than most comedy festivals see in a decade. Pins & Needles Comedy \u2014 New York City's tattoo-culture stand-up showcase \u2014 just wrapped a run at the [Edinburgh Festival Fringe](https://www.edfringe.com), the biggest arts festival on the planet, and it did exactly what a good Fringe show is supposed to do: it made people who thought they'd seen every kind of comedy show admit they hadn't.\n\nFor anyone new to it, the premise is simple and a little insane: host Taylor Drew brings out heavily tattooed comics who strip down, show the work, tell the story behind it, and then launch straight into a set. It's part stand-up showcase, part living gallery, and it only works if the comics are willing to actually be that exposed \u2014 literally and otherwise. At Edinburgh, they were.\n\n## Why This Show, Why This Festival\n\nThe Fringe isn't just another comedy stop. It's three weeks, thousands of shows, every discipline you can name packed into one city \u2014 the same festival that launched Fleabag onto the world stage. Dropping a scrappy, New York-born tattoo-and-comedy hybrid into that lineup is a real swing. Pins & Needles Comedy took it, landing a 13-night residency at The Raging Bull, August 6 through August 18, in the 22:15 slot \u2014 late enough that the room already knew what it signed up for. 18+, no exceptions.\n\n## Inside the Run\n\nFour of those thirteen nights \u2014 August 7, 13, 14, and 16 \u2014 had their lineups completely booked out well ahead of the run. And because every comic on the bill is working from their own ink and their own story, no two nights played the same. That's the mechanic that makes this show hard to replicate: the material is quite literally different every time, because the canvas is different every time.\n\nThe whole residency was also filmed professionally, which means footage from Edinburgh is headed to Pins & Needles Comedy's channels in the near future.\n\n## What Audience Members Said\n\n> \"I've seen a lot of stand-up at Fringe, but never this much skin and ink. Wildly funny and completely unapologetic.\" \u2014 Audience member, August 8th\n\n> \"Taylor keeps the energy high and the crowd roaring. The exact kind of late-night chaos you want at a comedy festival.\" \u2014 Audience member, August 10th\n\n> \"Come for the amazing tattoo art, stay because you're laughing too hard to leave. A brilliant concept.\" \u2014 Audience member, August 12th\n\n> \"Raw, hilarious, and literally stripped down. Hands down the most unique showcase I've been to this year.\" \u2014 Audience member, August 14th\n\n> \"If you think you've seen every type of comedy show, you haven't seen this. Great comics, great art, zero inhibitions.\" \u2014 Audience member, August 16th\n\n## FAQ\n\n## What is Pins & Needles Comedy?\n\nA New York City stand-up showcase where heavily tattooed comics show their ink, tell the story behind it, and then do a set. Hosted by Taylor Drew.\n\n## Did Pins & Needles Comedy perform at the Edinburgh Fringe?\n\nYes \u2014 13 nights at The Raging Bull during the 2026 Edinburgh Festival Fringe, August 6\u201318, with four nights booked completely full.\n\n## Who hosts Pins & Needles Comedy?\n\nTaylor Drew.",
