    title: "Pins & Needles Comedy Audition Open Mic \u2014 June 25th at 9 PM",
    date: "2026-06-20",
    excerpt: "Pins & Needles Comedy is throwing an audition open mic, and we want to see what you've got. Tattooed, non-tattooed, brand new, ten years deep \u2014 all comics welcome. You get five minutes to show us\u2026",
    body: "## Pins & Needles Comedy Audition Open Mic \u2014 June 25th\n\nTattoos and tight five. That is the whole pitch.\n\nPins & Needles Comedy is throwing an audition open mic, and we want to see what you've got. Tattooed, non-tattooed, brand new, ten years deep \u2014 all comics welcome. You get five minutes to show us your best stuff.\n\n## The details\n\n**Thursday, June 25th at 9 PM**\n\nFive minutes a comic. Sign up, go up, do your set. Comics may be selected for next month's Pins & Needles show, so this is your shot to get on the lineup.\n\n## Auditioning or just running a set \u2014 both work\n\nHere's the part people get nervous about: you do **not** have to be auditioning to get up. If you just want a spot to work out new material, run a set, or knock the rust off, come do the mic. No pressure, no audition required.\n\nAnd to clear up the tagline before anyone shows up confused \u2014 \"Strip Down for Stand Up\" is the bit, not the dress code. You do **not** need to strip down for the audition mic. Keep your clothes on. Just bring the jokes.\n\n## Why this mic\n\nPins & Needles is built for comics who like their comedy a little louder and a little weirder. The audition mic is the front door. Whether you're trying to lock a spot on next month's show or you just want stage time, this is an easy, low-stakes room to do exactly that.\n\nCome get your five.\n\n**All comics welcome. Thursday, June 25th. 9 PM.**",
